  "body": "Sub-issue of #102. Design: `docs/design-history/2026-08-05-coding-agents-and-tools.md`.\n\nA hand-rolled client in `crates/epik` beside `chat.rs`, on the `OpenAiCompatible` precedent: synchronous, no SDK crate (`octocrab` rejected — async/tokio against a synchronous library, and it misses the GraphQL mutations anyway). REST for issues (get/create/edit/comment/close), PRs (open/get/merge), check conclusions, default branch; GraphQL (POST `/graphql`) for sub-issue add/remove and blocked-by set/remove. The surface covers exactly Epik's verbs, nothing more. Typed errors, with rate limiting distinguished from failure. Stringliness confined to the module.\n\nTesting, shaped by secretless CI: a unit tier against captured payloads; an unauthenticated read smoke against this public repo in CI; mutation tests run locally against a scratch repo only when a token is present, and are required nowhere — no secret enters CI.\n\nAcceptance: the parent feature's acceptance list is achievable through this module alone.",
